    vex:statusNotes """
        Only present via gvfs (SMB client for Nautilus 'Other Locations').
        The bug is in the server-side vfs_worm VFS module; we never run smbd/nmbd.
        """ .


# ── Fixed in the version we run, or patched by Nixpkgs without a version change ───

triage:brotli-1.2.1
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/brotli@1.2.1> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-111497 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        NVD CPE false positive: 1.2.1 is the release that fixes this CVE.
        The record lists Google Brotli as affected from 1.0.3 up to 1.0.10, from 1.1.0 up to 1.1.1 and from 1.2.0 up to 1.2.1, so 1.2.1 is outside every range.
        It also lists an unrelated Go port, andybalholm/brotli, affected below 1.2.7. vulnix reports 1.2.1 anyway, and the Go port's range is the likely match, because it compares the product name and version and not the vendor.
        In CISA KEV since 2026-10-27; its notes name the v1.2.1 release as the fix, which agrees with this assessment.
        """ .

