    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/libssh2@1.11.1> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2025-15661 , nvd:CVE-2026-55199 , nvd:CVE-2026-55200 , nvd:CVE-2026-58050 , nvd:CVE-2026-58051 , nvd:CVE-2026-66032 , nvd:CVE-2026-66033 , nvd:CVE-2026-66034 , nvd:CVE-2026-66035 , nvd:CVE-2026-7598 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        nixpkgs libssh2.patches carries a CVE patch for each of these ten.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:perl-5.42.3-fixed
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/perl@5.42.3> , <pkg:nix/perl@5.42.3-env> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-57432 , nvd:CVE-2026-13221 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        CVE-2026-57432's vulnerable range ends before 5.42.3-RC1; we run 5.42.3 final, which already contains the fix.
        CVE-2026-13221 (regex trie offset overflow with >65535 alternation branches) is fixed upstream in 5.43.10 by commit 03f74bb and backported to 5.42.3: regcomp_study.c in the nixpkgs 5.42.3 source has the `tail - startbranch >= U16_MAX` guard (GH #23388).
        The CPAN Security Group advisory gives the affected range as "through 5.43.9", so the flag on 5.42.3 is a false positive.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:unzip-6.0
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/unzip@6.0> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2021-4217 , nvd:CVE-2022-0529 , nvd:CVE-2022-0530 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Already patched in nixpkgs: unzip.patches includes CVE-2021-4217.patch and 28-cve-2022-0529-and-cve-2022-0530.patch.
        Upstream Info-ZIP never released a fixed version (last release ~2009), so the version string still reads 6.0 and vulnix's version-based matching can't see the applied patches.
        """ .


triage:dnsmasq-2.93
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/dnsmasq@2.93> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-6507 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        grype gives the fix as 2.93test9, a test release before 2.93, and doesn't order the final 2.93 after it.
        2.93 is the release that followed the test series, so it contains the fix for this BOOTREPLY out-of-bounds write.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .

triage:firefox-bundled-harfbuzz
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/firefox> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2011-0064 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Found only by grype, because the NVD record lists mozilla:firefox with no version bound.
        The bug is a missing allocation check in hb_buffer_ensure in HarfBuzz, as Pango 1.28.3 and Firefox shipped it in 2011, and HarfBuzz fixed it that year.
        Firefox bundles a current HarfBuzz, and the system harfbuzz is 14.5.1.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .

triage:firefox-old-unbounded-records
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/firefox> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2003-1492 , nvd:CVE-2007-1970 , nvd:CVE-2007-2176 , nvd:CVE-2007-3827 , nvd:CVE-2007-5967 , nvd:CVE-2007-6715 , nvd:CVE-2009-4129 , nvd:CVE-2009-4130 , nvd:CVE-2009-4630 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Found only by grype, because each NVD record lists Firefox with no version bound, so it matches every release.
        They are Firefox and Mozilla bugs from 2003 to 2009: a cookie domain with a trailing dot, mixed-content warnings for dynamically written elements, an unspecified JavaScript-error bug, domainless cookies, embedded certificate installation, a crash on a crafted GIF, two script-dialog origin spoofs, and DNS prefetching from local HTML, which Mozilla disputed.
        Firefox 160 is about 13 to 23 years and over 150 major releases later.
        This rests on that age and the unbounded records, not on a fix traced for each CVE: none of the records names a fixed version.
        Re-checked against NVD on 2026-11-22.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .

triage:glibc-2.44-57-release
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/glibc@2.44-57> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-6791 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        grype gives the fix as glibc 2.44, the release this package is built from: 2.44-57 is 2.44 with 57 commits from the release branch.
        grype reads 2.44-57 as earlier than 2.44, so it reports the tilde-expansion bug in parse_tilde as open.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .

triage:imagemagick-7.1.2-35
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/imagemagick@7.1.2-35> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2023-5341 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        NVD lists ImageMagick as affected before 7.1.2, and this is 7.1.2-35, the 35th patch release of 7.1.2.
        grype reads 7.1.2-35 as earlier than 7.1.2, so it reports this 2023 use-after-free in coders/bmp.c as open.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .

triage:libtpms-0.10.2-unstable-2026-05-06
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/libtpms@0.10.2-unstable-2026-05-06> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-21444 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        The bug affects 0.10.0 and 0.10.1, and 0.10.2 fixes it with commit 33c9ff0 on the stable branch.
        Nixpkgs builds a snapshot of the main branch (521c510, 6 May 2026), which diverged from 0.10.2, so that commit isn't in its history.
        The same fix ("tpm2: Fix retrieval of updated IV when using OpenSSL >= 3.0") landed on the main branch as ee31b0b on 29 December 2025, which the snapshot contains.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/stefanberger/libtpms/security/advisories/GHSA-7jxr-4j3g-p34f> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .

triage:linux-jfs-2020
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/linux> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2020-27815 ;
    vex:status "fixed" ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        A JFS bug from 2020, fixed in mainline Linux 5.11 and backported to the 4.9 to 5.10 long-term kernels.
        grype lists only those backports as fixed versions, so it reports every later kernel line as open.
        Every kernel this repository builds is newer than 5.11, so the statement covers every version.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/pull/145> .


# ── Affected: real, unpatched and accepted as low risk until a fix lands ──────

triage:avahi-0.8
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/avahi@0.8> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2025-59529 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-20"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        avahi-daemon runs (GNOME service discovery).
        The simple-protocol server ignores its client limit, allowing a local user to exhaust connections: local DoS only, single-user machine.
        Re-checked on 2026-11-22: the v0.8 source defines CLIENTS_MAX in avahi-daemon/simple-protocol.c but never checks it, so 0.8 is affected.
        The nixpkgs package carries a note that this CVE 'is introduced by 4e2e1ea', but that commit only touches avahi-core/wide-area.c, so the note does not make 0.8 a false positive.
        NVD lists no fixed release (affected through 0.9-rc5), and nixpkgs ships 0.8 with no patch for it.
        Renewed for four weeks given the low impact.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        do not give untrusted users a local account or run untrusted code on this machine; if mDNS (.local) lookups stop working, restart avahi-daemon.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:binutils-2.46
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/binutils@2.46> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-6846 , nvd:CVE-2025-69649 , nvd:CVE-2025-69650 , nvd:CVE-2025-69651 , nvd:CVE-2025-69652 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-11-26"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Pulled in via gcc, which LazyVim's nvim-treesitter uses to compile parsers from source fetched by lazy.nvim.
        CVE-2026-6846 needs linking a crafted XCOFF (AIX) object file; nothing here links XCOFF.
        It is confirmed unfixed in 2.46 (bfd/xcofflink.c still sizes reloc_info by section_count + 1) and fixed in 2.47.
        CVE-2025-69649/69650/69651/69652 are readelf crashes (DoS only) on crafted ELF input; readelf is never run on untrusted binaries.
        Debian's tracker lists fix commits for these tagged binutils-2_46, but each description says affected 'thru 2.46', so whether the nixpkgs 2.46 tarball already contains them is unverified.
        Accepted risk; drop this entry once nixpkgs ships binutils 2.47, and re-check before it expires.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        Do not run readelf or objdump on untrusted binaries, and do not link object files from untrusted sources, until nixpkgs ships binutils 2.47.
        """ .

triage:cfitsio-4.7.0
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/cfitsio@4.7.0> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-111124 , nvd:CVE-2026-111125 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-20"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Real and unpatched: heap out-of-bounds reads on a crafted FITS (astronomy image) file, one through a zero or negative ZDITHER0 seed in the imcompress.c unquantize helpers and one in the HCOMPRESS tile decoder (fits_hdecompress.c).
        A crash or a small heap leak at worst (CVSS 6.1, local, needs a user to open the file).
        NVD lists 4.7.0, the latest release, as affected.
        Upstream master has HCOMPRESS bounds checking (commit b07f2e4c, 2026-11-02), which looks like the fix for CVE-2026-111125, but there is no release yet; nixpkgs ships 4.7.0 with a patch only for CVE-2026-115504. cfitsio joined the closure on 2026-11-22 with appstream 1.2.3, through vips: the only file in appstream that references vips is lib/ascompose/asc-mediaworker, the helper `appstreamcli compose` uses to process icons and screenshots when building catalogue metadata for a software repository. libappstream, which GNOME apps use to read metadata, does not link vips, and nothing here runs `appstreamcli compose`.
        Accepted as low risk.
        Re-check for a cfitsio release after 4.7.0 before this expires.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        do not run `appstreamcli compose` or the vips command-line tools on FITS files or software metadata from untrusted sources.
        """ .

triage:cjson-1.7.19
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/cjson@1.7.19> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-67215 , nvd:CVE-2026-67216 , nvd:CVE-2026-67217 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-20"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        All in cJSON_Utils (RFC 6902 JSON Patch / cJSON_Compare): stack exhaustion, exponential compare time, non-atomic patch.
        Needs an application applying an untrusted JSON Patch: DoS at worst.
        Re-checked on 2026-11-22: nixpkgs still ships 1.7.19 with no patches.
        Renewed for four weeks given the low impact.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        do not feed JSON Patch documents or JSON for comparison from untrusted sources to tools built on cJSON.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:cups-2.4.19-unpatched
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/cups@2.4.19> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-55480 , nvd:CVE-2026-61702 , nvd:CVE-2026-107888 , nvd:CVE-2026-55453 , nvd:CVE-2026-107885 , nvd:CVE-2026-107890 , nvd:CVE-2026-55467 , nvd:CVE-2026-107886 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-11-27"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        These eight are real but are all in the cupsd scheduler or the IPP backend (CVE-2026-55480 symlink race, 61702 path traversal, 55453 and 55467 option injection, 107888, 107885, 107890 and 107886 denial of service); they are fixed in CUPS 2.4.20 (CVE-2026-107885 needs 2.4.21), but nixpkgs still ships 2.4.19. services.printing is disabled, so cupsd never runs; only the libcups client library stays in the closure, pulled in by GTK, Qt and similar.
        None of these bugs are in libcups.
        Accepted as low risk.
        Re-check for a CUPS 2.4.21 bump in nixpkgs before this expires.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        do not re-enable services.printing until a fixed CUPS lands, and do not run cupsd or open IPP (port 631) in the meantime.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:dhcpcd-10.3.2
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/dhcpcd@10.3.2> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-56113 , nvd:CVE-2026-56114 , nvd:CVE-2026-56116 , nvd:CVE-2026-56117 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-20"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Fixes land after 10.3.2. dhcpcd is in the closure only as a NetworkManager dependency; the dhcpcd service is inactive and NetworkManager uses its internal DHCP client, so neither the same-link DHCPv6/RA bugs nor the control-socket bug are reachable.
        Re-checked on 2026-11-22: nixpkgs still ships 10.3.2 with no patches.
        Renewed for four weeks because the code isn't reachable.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        do not enable networking.dhcpcd or switch NetworkManager's DHCP client to dhcpcd until a fixed release lands.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:ffmpeg-9.0.2-unpatched
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/ffmpeg@9.0.2> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-107675 , nvd:CVE-2026-107676 , nvd:CVE-2026-107677 , nvd:CVE-2026-107678 , nvd:CVE-2026-107696 , nvd:CVE-2026-125064 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-06"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        CVE-2026-107675/107676/107677/107678/107696 (SFTP host-key check, uninitialised metadata bytes, DASH and RTSP infinite loops, stack exhaustion on a crafted MP4) are described by NVD as affecting releases through 9.0.2, though its CPE range stops before 9.0.2, so whether 9.0.2 is really affected is unclear; there is no later release and nixos-unstable ships 9.0.2.
        CVE-2026-107660, which the 9.0.1 entry covered, is fixed in 9.0.2.
        CVE-2026-125064 (added 2026-11-22) is a NULL pointer dereference in the G.726 decoder (libavcodec/g726.c ignores an init_get_bits() failure) on a crafted AVI with an oversized G.726 audio chunk: a crash only.
        NVD lists it as affecting releases through 9.0.2, the fix (commit ec887b1) is on master only, and nixpkgs carries no patch for it.
        All real or presumed real, and accepted as low risk: each needs ffmpeg to process hostile media or connect to a hostile server, and ffmpeg is only in the closure as a library dependency of desktop apps; no scripts or services here feed it untrusted URLs.
        Renewed on 2026-11-22 for two weeks, because nixos-unstable still ships 9.0.2 and the highest CVSS is 8.8.
        Re-check for an ffmpeg bump in nixpkgs before this expires.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        until nixpkgs ships a fixed ffmpeg, do not play, transcode or thumbnail media from untrusted sources with ffmpeg or apps built on it (especially RTSP, DASH or sftp URLs, and MP4 or MKV files from unknown senders).
        Stick to media you trust.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:libsndfile-1.2.2-unpatched
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/libsndfile@1.2.2> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2024-50613 , nvd:CVE-2025-52194 , nvd:CVE-2025-56226 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-06"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        No release since 1.2.2, and Nixpkgs has no patch for these three (re-checked on 2026-11-22).
        All need a crafted audio file opened by an app using libsndfile;
        CVE-2025-52194 (IRCAM header overflow, CVSS 7.5) is the most serious.
        Accepted as low risk; renewed for two weeks given that CVSS.
        Drop this statement when a fixed libsndfile lands.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        do not open untrusted IRCAM, WAV or AIFF files in apps that use libsndfile; stick to audio from sources you trust.
        """ ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/huwd/declarative_laptop/issues/17> .

triage:rsync-3.5.0
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/rsync@3.5.0> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-119741 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-12-06"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Real and unpatched: in the delta-transfer sender, hash_search() does unbounded strong-checksum work when a malicious receiver sends weak checksums that collide at consecutive offsets, exhausting CPU (denial of service only, CVSS 7.5).
        NVD gives the fix as 3.5.2, though its CPE range stops at 3.5.1; nixpkgs ships 3.5.0 on nixos-unstable and master with no patches.
        It is the sender that is affected, and the realistic target is a public rsync daemon module.
        We run no rsync daemon and only use rsync as a client over ssh.
        Accepted as low risk; renewed on 2026-11-22 for two weeks because nixpkgs is still on 3.5.0.
        Re-check for an rsync bump in nixpkgs before this expires.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        until a fixed rsync lands, do not run rsyncd or serve a module to the network, and do not let untrusted hosts pull from this machine with rsync.
        """ .

triage:sqlite-3.54.0
    a triage:Statement ;
    vex:product <pkg:nix/sqlite@3.54.0> ;
    vex:vulnerability nvd:CVE-2026-119586 ;
    vex:status "affected" ;
    triage:until "2026-11-27"^^xsd:date ;
    vex:statusNotes """
        Real and unpatched: the sqlite3 shell's .recover command prints attacker-planted dot-commands from a database's schema verbatim, so a crafted database can run shell commands when the output of .recover is piped back into sqlite3 (CVSS 7.8, local, needs a user to run it).
        NVD says it affects SQLite through 3.54.1, the newest release, so no fixed version exists, and nixpkgs ships 3.54.0 on nixos-unstable and master.
        The other ten CVEs accepted under sqlite-3.53.3 are fixed in 3.54.0.
        Library use isn't affected, the sqlite3 shell isn't in the system profile (user profiles weren't checked), and we do not open untrusted databases.
        Accepted as low risk.
        Re-check for a release after 3.54.1 before this expires.
        """ ;
    vex:actionStatement """
        never run .recover on a database you did not create, and never pipe its output into sqlite3 or a shell.
        """ .
